From: =?UTF-8?q?Ond=C5=99ej=20=C5=A0imon?= <ondrej@dorhawk.software>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:14:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 80/81] winemac.drv: Keep a minimized window's picture for the
 Dock.

Windows redraws a window it minimizes at its parked size, 160x31 at
-32000, and the new small surface's flush replaced the Mac window's
picture: the Dock showed a blank window with a dash, and the restored
window came back with it. While the window is minimized, a flush no
longer changes the Mac window's picture.

Tried with Enterprise Architect: minimized, the Dock shows its window;
before, a dash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/surface.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/surface.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/surface.c
index bdbcdcdfe6..08d0f32686 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/surface.c
@@ -84,6 +84,16 @@ static BOOL macdrv_surface_flush(struct window_surface *window_surface, const RE
     CGColorSpaceRef colorspace;
     CGImageRef image;
     struct macdrv_win_data *data;
+    BOOL minimized = FALSE;
+
+    /* Windows draws a window it minimized at its small parked size. The Mac window keeps the
+     * picture it had: the Dock shows it, and it comes back with the window. */
+    if ((data = get_win_data(window_surface->hwnd)))
+    {
+        minimized = data->minimized;
+        release_win_data(data);
+    }
+    if (minimized) return TRUE;
 
     colorspace = CGColorSpaceCreateWithName(kCGColorSpaceSRGB);
     image = CGImageCreate(color_info->bmiHeader.biWidth, abs(color_info->bmiHeader.biHeight), 8, 32,
